# fixedbugs, defect 143, panel 185 R1, lane ffi-macro, 2026-10-02.
#
# SYMPTOM: `function WEXITSTATUS(status: i32) -> i64` under `extern
# "sys/wait.h"` was `ffi_unknown_name`, *`sys/wait.h` declares no
# `WEXITSTATUS`*, though the header defines it, as a macro, on macOS and on
# glibc alike.
#
# CAUSE: the probe calls its callee in parentheses (panel 092), which is what
# holds a fortified `memset` to its widths, and a parenthesised name expands
# no function-like macro, so clang called it undeclared. And a macro has no
# parameter types: panel 185 measured that a call through it holds none of
# them, `status: u8` reading four bytes of one.
#
# FIX: the round clang refused asks the header, once, which of its names are
# macros (`emit/ffi_asked.hero`), and such a name is `ffi_macro_name`: told
# as a macro, with the repair, a function of the program's own that calls it,
# drafted with placeholders for every C type. Skipped where the machine has
# no `sys/wait.h`.

extern "sys/wait.h"
    function WEXITSTATUS(status: i32) -> i64  #~ ffi_macro_name

function main()
    print(WEXITSTATUS(status: 256))
